  "worked_solution": "Let $A$ denote the area under the curve $y=v(t)$ over $[0,1.5].$ \nIn this case, we have $n=5$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the total distance traveled can be approximated as\n\n$$\nA\u2248v(0.3)\u0394{t}_{1}+v(0.7)\u0394{t}_{2}+v(1)\u0394{t}_{3}+v(1.3)\u0394{t}_{4}+v(1.5)\u0394{t}_{5},\n$$\n\nwhere each $\u0394{t}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $t$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\u0394{t}_{i}={t}_{i}-{t}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $\u0394t$'s.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ | $1.3$ | $1.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\u0394t$ | $-$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $v(t)$ | $-$ | $35$ | $40$ | $65$ | $80$ | $65$ |\n\nWe plug in the numbers to approximate the number of liters and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u224835\\cdot 0.3+40\\cdot 0.4+65\\cdot 0.3+80\\cdot 0.3+65\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =10.5+16+19.5+24+13 \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total distance traveled by the boat. So, the distance is approximately $83\\,\\text{mi}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
